## 💡 Why This Exists
Most AI homework helpers encourage cheating by instantly spitting out the final answer. **Live AI Vision Tutor** acts like a real human teacher: it looks at your notebook via your live camera feed, catches your exact calculation mistakes, and asks **Socratic guiding questions** to help you figure out the next step yourself.

## ✨ Key Features
* **👀 Live Vision:** Point your phone camera or webcam at your textbook or handwritten math problems.
* **🗣️ Voice-Activated:** Speak naturally to the tutor using browser voice recognition; it talks back using text-to-speech.
* **🚫 Anti-Cheat Logic:** System instructions force the AI to *never* give direct answers—only hints and error-checking.
* **💸 100% Free Stack:** Built using browser APIs and Google AI Studio's free tier. No server costs or paid subscriptions required.

---

## 🛠️ Tech Stack
* **Frontend:** Vanilla HTML5, CSS3, JavaScript
* **AI Brain:** Google Gemini API (`gemini-2.5-flash`) via REST
* **Vision:** HTML5 MediaDevices API (`navigator.mediaDevices.getUserMedia`)
* **Ears & Voice:** Web Speech API & SpeechSynthesis
* **Hosting:** GitHub Pages (HTTPS secured)

---

## 🚀 How to Run It Yourself (Locally or Deployed)

1. **Get a Free API Key:**
   * Head over to [Google AI Studio](https://aistudio.google.com).
   * Create a free API key.

2. **Clone or Copy:**
   * Download or copy the `index.html` file from this repository.

3. **Open & Test:**
   * Open `index.html` in any modern mobile browser (Chrome/Safari).
   * Enter your Gemini API key in the password field.
   * Allow camera and microphone permissions, point at your homework, and start talking!

